title: Vilnius Question
subtitle: The Republic of **<span style="color: #D00;">Central Lithuania</span>** has adopted a motion to incorporate itself to the <b><span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Polish </span><span style="color: #DC143C;">Republic</span>**
tags: event
is-card: true
on-arrival: vilnius_seen = 1; president_confidence -= 20
face-image: img/vilnius.png
view-if: vilnius_seen = 0 and year = 1922 and month >= 3
new-page: true

= Vilnius Question

On the 20th of February 1922, the Seimas of **<span style="color: #DD0000;">Central Lithuania</span>** adopted a resolution declaring the Vilnius Region an inseparable part of the Republic of **<span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>**. The motion passed by 96 votes to none, with six abstentions, rejecting all foreign claims to the territory and requesting its immediate incorporation into the **<span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** state.

*“The Vilnius Land constitutes, without conditions or reservations, an inseparable part of the Repubic of **<span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>**”* — Point 4 of the resolution

Diplomatic representatives accredited in **<span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>** warned the authorities against the "disastrous impression" that would be created by the simple incorporation of Vilnius.

- @government_stance

@government_stance
title: The **<span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** Government Responds.

The Government of [+ prime_minister +] have submitted a draft "Act of Incorporation" to supplement the motion proposed by **<span style="color: #D00;">Central Lithuania</span>** which grants the Republic of **<span style="color: #D00;">Central Lithuania</span>** autonomy similar to that enjoyed by the Silesian Vovoideship

- @reject

@reject
title: The Draft is Rejected.

The **<span style="color: #D00;">Central Lithuania</span>** delegates have rejected the amendment, insisting that the Vilnius Region be incorprated to the **<span style="color: #CCCCCC;">Polish </span><span style="color: #DC143C;">Republic</span>** without conditions.

Due to the delegates refusal to amend the resolution, it culminated into a political crises which led to the loss of trust in the government followed by the resignation of [+ prime_minister +] as Prime Minister.

President [+ president +] appoints the PSL-P and ZLN to form a government, however, ZLN refuses to form a cabinet and the PSL-P refuses to form a cabinet without support from the NPR, since the NPR hesitated to join a government with the National Democrats due to political disagreement...

- @deadlock

@deadlock
title: The Sejm is deadlocked.
subtitle: [+ president +] appoints [+ prime_minister +] again as a non-parliamentary candidate

[+ prime_minister +] recieved broad support in the Sejm from the NPR, PSL-P, PSL-W, and Other parties, however the Government lacks a stable majority.

As usual our party has extended their support to the government and tolerated it.

- @cabinet

@cabinet
title: [+ prime_minister +] appoints the ministers.
on-arrival: other_in_government = 0; other_toleration = 1; economic_minister = 'Ossowski'; interior_minister = 'Kamieński'


The <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">NZL<span class="wide_tooltip-tip">Extra-parliamentary party consisting of centre-right members.</span></span> (Extra-parliamentary) who have previously been in government have been omitted out of the government.

The following ministry has been shuffled: The Economic Minister and the Interior Minister.

@finalized
title: The new government is finalized

The new government is finalized, we wait on how [+ prime_minister +] and his cabinet would approach the Question of Vilnius.
